      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\nThere is a potential bug here: `data-\u003eall_protected \u003d 0;` is cleared unconditionally before verifying that `flash_set_status(dev, sr1, sr2)` successfully applies the hardware state. If the status write fails, this leaves the software state incorrectly downgraded without the hardware state actually changing. Clear `all_protected` only upon success. \n\nAdditionally, consider using `uint8_t` for `reg1` and `reg2` to match the types of `sr1` and `sr2` and the arguments provided by callers.\n\n```c\nstatic int flash_set_status_for_prot(const struct device *dev, uint8_t reg1,\n\t\t\t\t     uint8_t reg2)\n{\n\tstruct cros_flash_rtkfp_data *data \u003d DRV_DATA(dev);\n\tuint8_t sr1, sr2;\n\tint ret;\n\n\tflash_get_status(dev, \u0026sr1, \u0026sr2);\n\n\tsr1 \u0026\u003d ~(SPI_FLASH_SR1_BP0 | SPI_FLASH_SR1_BP1 | SPI_FLASH_SR1_BP2 |\n\t\t SPI_FLASH_SR1_TB | SPI_FLASH_SR1_SEC);\n\tsr2 \u0026\u003d ~SPI_FLASH_SR2_CMP;\n\n\tsr1 |\u003d reg1;\n\tsr2 |\u003d reg2;\n\n\tret \u003d flash_set_status(dev, sr1, sr2);\n\tif (ret \u003d\u003d EC_SUCCESS) {\n\t\tdata-\u003eall_protected \u003d 0;\n\t}\n\treturn ret;\n}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/71f17ada-46ae-46aa-9023-1b355efebfa8)",
