      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\nThe `#ifdef` blocks splitting `} else if {` chains are brittle and increase cognitive load. Since the flash layout is strictly layered (`WP_STORAGE` -\u003e `ROLLBACK` -\u003e `RW_MEM`), any region ending beyond a higher boundary inherently covers the lower boundaries. You can eliminate the `else if` chains completely by evaluating each boundary independently, making the code more robust and declarative without preprocessor token-stitching.\n\n```c\n\t/* Check if ranges fully overlap. This logic assumes a certain flash\n\t * layout: RO -\u003e ROLLBACKS -\u003e RW.\n\t */\n\tif (prot_end \u003e\u003d (CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_OFF + CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_SIZE)) {\n\t\tflags |\u003d EC_FLASH_PROTECT_RO_AT_BOOT;\n\t}\n#ifdef CONFIG_ROLLBACK\n\tif (prot_end \u003e\u003d (CONFIG_ROLLBACK_OFF + CONFIG_ROLLBACK_SIZE)) {\n\t\tflags |\u003d EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ROLLBACK_AT_BOOT;\n\t}\n#endif /* CONFIG_ROLLBACK */\n\tif (prot_end \u003e\u003d (CONFIG_RW_MEM_OFF + CONFIG_RW_SIZE)) {\n\t\tflags |\u003d EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ALL_AT_BOOT;\n\t}\n\n\t/* Software protection is enabled. Add proper _NOW flags. */\n\tif (data-\u003esw_protected) {\n\t\tif (flags \u0026 EC_FLASH_PROTECT_RO_AT_BOOT) {\n\t\t\tflags |\u003d EC_FLASH_PROTECT_RO_NOW;\n\t\t}\n#ifdef CONFIG_ROLLBACK\n\t\tif (flags \u0026 EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ROLLBACK_AT_BOOT) {\n\t\t\tflags |\u003d EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ROLLBACK_NOW;\n\t\t}\n#endif /* CONFIG_ROLLBACK */\n\t\tif (flags \u0026 EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ALL_AT_BOOT) {\n\t\t\tflags |\u003d EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ALL_NOW;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/71f17ada-46ae-46aa-9023-1b355efebfa8)",
